      "phase_evolution": {
        "value": "During intercritical annealing, portions of bainite and martensite re-austenitize due to the high solubility of carbon in austenite, leading to carbon enrichment and enhanced stability; carbon-depleted regions form ferrite, some carbon-enriched austenite is retained on cooling as RA, unstabilized austenite transforms diffusionlessly to fresh martensite, and bainite forms in regions not fully austenitized.",
